# Merge-conflict debris. Two of these (648 lines) reached main via #237, and #238
# was closed partly for committing a third. Nothing ignored them, so nothing stopped
# them.
*.orig
*.rej

# Orphaned declaration source maps. 513 of these were committed under package src/
# dirs (none had a matching .d.ts). .gitignore only covered dist/, so anything a
# build left in src/ was committable. NOT *.d.ts - those are real ambient decls.
*.d.ts.map
*.js.map

# Output of the external `repo-tools map`. No generator, consumer or gate of this repository uses
# them.
docs/Architecture/dependency-layers.json
docs/Architecture/unused-analysis.json

# Generated by `bun run docs:deps`; not committed. A pull request that adds a file or an export
# changes several of these files, so a committed copy makes two such pull requests conflict.
# A new checkout has none of them: run `bun run build` and then `bun run docs:deps`. The gates
# that read them run in the hook and in CI right after `docs:deps` writes them. CI fails when
# git tracks one of them. The hand-kept files of docs/Architecture, `coverage-policy.json`,
# `COVERAGE_POLICY.md`, `duplicate-baseline.json` and `duplicate-backlog.md` stay committed.
docs/Architecture/FILE_INVENTORY.md
docs/Architecture/file-inventory.json
docs/Architecture/TEST_COVERAGE.md
docs/Architecture/test-coverage.json
docs/Architecture/DEPENDENCY_GRAPH.md
docs/Architecture/dependency-graph.json
docs/Architecture/dependency-graph.yaml
docs/Architecture/dependency-summary.compact.json
docs/Architecture/dependency-reverse.json
docs/Architecture/node-safety.json
docs/Architecture/package-export-surfaces.json
docs/Architecture/unused-analysis.md
docs/Architecture/duplicate-symbols.json
docs/Architecture/duplicate-symbols.md
